WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.320
There are so many new beauty releases

00:00:02.320 --> 00:00:03.653
happening all the time,

00:00:03.653 --> 00:00:05.842
so we gathered some of
the most-hyped products

00:00:05.842 --> 00:00:07.170
to test for ourselves.

00:00:07.170 --> 00:00:11.700
We have yet another
color-changing product to review.

00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:13.234
This is the Kylie Cosmetics

00:00:13.234 --> 00:00:14.936
transformative liquid lip tint

00:00:14.936 --> 00:00:17.790
that was a part of her
collab with the Wizard of Oz.

00:00:17.790 --> 00:00:20.490
It goes from emerald green to pink.

00:00:20.490 --> 00:00:21.780
The smell is interesting.

00:00:21.780 --> 00:00:24.570
It kind of smells like an apple-y shampoo.

00:00:24.570 --> 00:00:26.220
The formula is pretty thin.

00:00:26.220 --> 00:00:28.320
I do like this giant doe-foot applicator.

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:30.300
The color is actually a little more unique

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:32.670
than other color-changing
lip products I've tried.

00:00:32.670 --> 00:00:34.618
The pink was a bit deeper and I think

00:00:34.618 --> 00:00:36.360
more flattering on my skin tone.

00:00:36.360 --> 00:00:37.768
I would wear this again because

00:00:37.768 --> 00:00:39.684
the stain it leaves behind is pretty,

00:00:39.684 --> 00:00:41.760
but I do wish the formula was thicker.

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:43.779
These are the Fleeky Friday Cosmetics

00:00:43.779 --> 00:00:45.480
Crystal Crease eyeliners.

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:48.330
These are handmade
reusable crystal eyeliners

00:00:48.330 --> 00:00:50.010
that you apply with lash glue.

00:00:50.010 --> 00:00:51.094
It was a little hard for me

00:00:51.094 --> 00:00:52.585
to get them in a comfortable spot,

00:00:52.585 --> 00:00:54.090
because I have hooded lids.

00:00:54.090 --> 00:00:56.048
You can cut these to fit
your eye shape better,

00:00:56.048 --> 00:00:57.360
so I'm going to do that next time,

00:00:57.360 --> 00:00:59.160
but I think these are so fun.

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:01.110
They look like you just did so much work

00:01:01.110 --> 00:01:03.450
applying each individual rhinestone.

00:01:03.450 --> 00:01:05.790
Cirque Colors is one of my
favorite nail-polish brands,

00:01:05.790 --> 00:01:07.800
and they just dropped
their holiday collection.

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:10.860
I love that they have a spin
on the classic red and green,

00:01:10.860 --> 00:01:12.350
this mix of pearly shades,

00:01:12.350 --> 00:01:14.610
and then this more unique duochrome.

00:01:14.610 --> 00:01:17.970
Sashay reminds me of red
bows and Christmas ornaments.

00:01:17.970 --> 00:01:19.980
To me it leans more pink than red,

00:01:19.980 --> 00:01:21.240
but it's still beautiful.

00:01:21.240 --> 00:01:23.220
Verdigris Jelly is a jelly polish.

00:01:23.220 --> 00:01:25.050
It is more sheer because it's a jelly,

00:01:25.050 --> 00:01:28.200
so I did three layers,
and it looked so shiny.

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:29.580
My favorite shade in the collection

00:01:29.580 --> 00:01:31.170
is definitely Tahitian Pearl,

00:01:31.170 --> 00:01:32.878
which is this dark duochrome

00:01:32.878 --> 00:01:34.728
that shifts from pink to green,

00:01:34.728 --> 00:01:36.840
and it has this holographic glitter in it.

00:01:36.840 --> 00:01:38.460
I did three coats for this one too

00:01:38.460 --> 00:01:40.170
because it showed the color shift better,

00:01:40.170 --> 00:01:42.330
and I think it made the glitter pop more.

00:01:42.330 --> 00:01:43.650
This is a really unique color,

00:01:43.650 --> 00:01:45.390
and I can see myself wearing it a lot.

00:01:45.390 --> 00:01:48.420
The last three shades are all
a pearlescent, sheer white

00:01:48.420 --> 00:01:50.190
with different-colored shimmers.

00:01:50.190 --> 00:01:51.990
Serenity has a green shimmer,

00:01:51.990 --> 00:01:54.030
Soleil has a pinky-red shimmer,

00:01:54.030 --> 00:01:55.920
and Siren has a purple shimmer.

00:01:55.920 --> 00:01:56.940
These are all really pretty,

00:01:56.940 --> 00:01:58.500
but you definitely don't need all of them,

00:01:58.500 --> 00:01:59.774
because they're so similar.

00:01:59.774 --> 00:02:01.920
This entire collection
applied really smoothly,

00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:03.780
and even though some shades
had to be layered up,

00:02:03.780 --> 00:02:05.610
I was happy with how they all turned out.

00:02:05.610 --> 00:02:08.790
This is the Half Magic
Magic Flik liquid eyeliner.

00:02:08.790 --> 00:02:11.940
It has this really interesting
tip that's paddle-shaped

00:02:11.940 --> 00:02:14.220
so you can draw fine lines with the edge

00:02:14.220 --> 00:02:16.290
and then fill in with the wide side.

00:02:16.290 --> 00:02:17.949
I suck at eyeliner, but this shape

00:02:17.949 --> 00:02:20.490
actually really helped
me draw the wing easily.

00:02:20.490 --> 00:02:23.340
I will say that I think
the actual eyeliner formula

00:02:23.340 --> 00:02:24.510
is not the best.

00:02:24.510 --> 00:02:27.510
The black isn't super
pigmented like I would prefer,

00:02:27.510 --> 00:02:29.400
but I really liked this tip shape.

00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:32.460
This is the KVD Dazzle
Long-Wear Eyeshadow Stick.

00:02:32.460 --> 00:02:35.130
It's supposed to be a
one-and-done-type product,

00:02:35.130 --> 00:02:36.660
so you don't need primer.

00:02:36.660 --> 00:02:38.550
You just swipe it on and blend.

00:02:38.550 --> 00:02:41.340
I was really surprised at
how soft this formula is.

00:02:41.340 --> 00:02:42.990
It's actually a little too soft,

00:02:42.990 --> 00:02:44.430
like, you have to be gentle with it,

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:46.440
but it really does glide on easily.

00:02:46.440 --> 00:02:48.540
This is packed with glitter and shimmer,

00:02:48.540 --> 00:02:50.550
and it just looks so pretty on the eyes.

00:02:50.550 --> 00:02:51.810
It's like a way to do glitter

00:02:51.810 --> 00:02:53.850
without any of the mess. I'm a fan.

00:02:53.850 --> 00:02:56.940
I tried a couple products from
the K-beauty brand Romand.

00:02:56.940 --> 00:02:58.920
This glitter palette has been raved about,

00:02:58.920 --> 00:03:00.990
so I was really excited to play with it.

00:03:00.990 --> 00:03:03.240
The shades are meant to be on the softer,

00:03:03.240 --> 00:03:04.590
more translucent side,

00:03:04.590 --> 00:03:06.750
so you can layer them over eye shadow.

00:03:06.750 --> 00:03:08.880
I just applied some of
my blush on the eyes

00:03:08.880 --> 00:03:11.220
and then applied a few
of the shades on top.

00:03:11.220 --> 00:03:12.660
There are shimmer formulas,

00:03:12.660 --> 00:03:15.195
fine glitters, and more chunky glitters.

00:03:15.195 --> 00:03:17.820
Overall, I would say the
formulas are on the dry side,

00:03:17.820 --> 00:03:20.010
but they were actually
pretty easy to work with.

00:03:20.010 --> 00:03:22.440
I had no problem swiping
or patting them on,

00:03:22.440 --> 00:03:24.660
and I had little to no glitter fallout.

00:03:24.660 --> 00:03:27.240
I also tried the Glasting Water Tint.

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:29.280
The color and gloss are separate layers,

00:03:29.280 --> 00:03:32.730
so you get that long-lasting
tint with a glossy finish.

00:03:32.730 --> 00:03:36.450
These feel so hydrating and
comfortable on the lips.

00:03:36.450 --> 00:03:37.380
They're really lightweight,

00:03:37.380 --> 00:03:39.270
and they definitely do leave a stain.

00:03:39.270 --> 00:03:41.785
Look at my hand after I
wiped those swatches off.

